626
00:37:30,563 --> 00:37:35,163
確かにここの堀を見つけられたら、地図だと分かりやすいもんね、水に囲まれてる地形って。
For sure, if I'd spotted this moat... terrain surrounded by water is so obvious on a map.

627
00:37:35,663 --> 00:37:37,363
それで分かったかも。
I might've figured it out from that.

628
00:37:37,563 --> 00:37:38,863
確かに！
Totally!

629
00:37:39,163 --> 00:37:40,463
あ、ちょっとこれ行けたな。
Ah, I could've gotten this one.

630
00:37:40,663 --> 00:37:42,363
これもうちょい絞れたな。
I could have narrowed it down more.

631
00:37:42,563 --> 00:37:45,963
だってほら、上から見てさ、すっごい分かりやすいもんね。
'Cause look, viewing it from above, it's super obvious.

632
00:37:46,663 --> 00:37:48,163
なるほどなー。
I see...

633
00:37:48,963 --> 00:37:51,563
いや、やっぱ歴史の勉強しとくべきだなー。
Man, I really should study history.

634
00:37:51,763 --> 00:37:54,963
あっ！「赤井ステーション」じゃって！赤井駅！
Ah! It says "Akai Station"! Akai Station!

635
00:37:55,563 --> 00:37:58,763
さあ赤井駅はどこだ？探すのじゃ。
Now then, where is Akai Station? Time to search!

636
00:37:59,363 --> 00:38:02,763
市民… 市民… 何市だ？何市だ？何県だ？
Citizen... Citizen... What city is this? What city? What prefecture?

637
00:38:03,363 --> 00:38:04,963
おっと？
Oops?

638
00:38:05,763 --> 00:38:07,363
ほっこり…か？
Hokkori... maybe?

639
00:38:07,663 --> 00:38:09,363
ほう、東北か？
Oh, Tohoku?

640
00:38:09,663 --> 00:38:12,663
とうほっ… ん？東北っぽくないか？
Touho-... Huh? Doesn't this look like Tohoku?

641
00:38:13,163 --> 00:38:15,163
東北の香り。
A whiff of Tohoku.

642
00:38:15,563 --> 00:38:17,963
北都オーディオ。
Hokuto Audio.

643
00:38:18,563 --> 00:38:20,363
東北の香り！
A whiff of Tohoku!

644
00:38:22,963 --> 00:38:25,663
東北の香りがするのじゃ。
I sense a Tohoku vibe!

645
00:38:26,163 --> 00:38:27,663
ほうほうほう。
I see, I see.

646
00:38:28,163 --> 00:38:30,963
他に見えるかな？なんかでも…
Can I see anything else? But somehow...

647
00:38:31,013 --> 00:38:33,163
ひらがなに見えない？なんとか市。
Doesn't that look like hiragana? "Something"-shi.

648
00:38:33,363 --> 00:38:36,163
いや、ちょっと… ちょっと見えないなー。
Wait, I can't... I can't quite see it.

649
00:38:36,263 --> 00:38:37,963
ちょっと見えないなー。
Can't quite read it.

650
00:38:38,163 --> 00:38:43,363
他に何か拾える情報があればいいんじゃけど。山とか見るか。東北なら山見るか、一旦。
If only there were other clues I could pick up. Let's look at the mountains. If it's Tohoku, let's check the mountains for a moment.

651
00:38:44,763 --> 00:38:46,963
一旦山…
Checking the mountains...

652
00:38:47,663 --> 00:38:51,163
西に山が結構あって、東は結構ないから、
There are quite a few mountains to the west, and hardly any to the east, so...

653
00:38:51,663 --> 00:38:56,763
太平洋側の海側？海側な気がする。
Pacific side, along the coast? I feel like it's on the coastal side.

654
00:38:57,563 --> 00:38:59,563
んで、寒さがどれぐらい…
And how cold is it...

655
00:38:59,763 --> 00:39:04,963
東北なんじゃけど、あんまり東北っぽい寒そうな感じがしないから、
It's Tohoku, but it doesn't give off that bitterly cold Tohoku vibe, so...

656
00:39:05,163 --> 00:39:08,663
あんま北の方じゃないのではと予想。
...I'm predicting it's not that far north.

657
00:39:08,963 --> 00:39:12,163
こういうとこなんじゃないかと予想するのじゃ。
I predict it's somewhere around here!

658
00:39:13,663 --> 00:39:14,963
んで…
And...

659
00:39:15,363 --> 00:39:17,163
他にヒントあるかな？
Are there any other clues?

660
00:39:17,663 --> 00:39:20,163
いやこれね、ひらがなっぽいんだよね。
No, this really looks like hiragana.

661
00:39:20,463 --> 00:39:27,163
だったら結構いわき市あると思っててね、わし。この、ここのさ、3文字のひらがな市に見えない？
In that case, I'm thinking Iwaki City is quite likely. Doesn't this... right here look like a three-character hiragana city name?

662
00:39:28,163 --> 00:39:30,663
から、多分いわき市… あ、あるやん！
So probably Iwaki Ci-... Ah, it's there!

663
00:39:31,163 --> 00:39:33,163
のじゃー！
Noja-!

664
00:39:35,163 --> 00:39:38,663
んで、駅が… ここか。だから西、西…
And the station is... here. So west, west...

665
00:39:40,163 --> 00:39:44,163
のいちゃ、のいちゃ。この辺か？
Let's see, let's see. Around here?

666
00:39:44,363 --> 00:39:46,663
あ、あった！北都オーディオ！
Ah, found it! Hokuto Audio!

667
00:39:46,963 --> 00:39:50,163
北都オーディオ… あれ、さっきどこで見たんじゃっけ、わしそれ？ここか。
Hokuto Audio... Wait, where did I see that earlier? Here?

668
00:39:50,663 --> 00:39:53,663
ど南、ど南にあった！そう、ここ！
Dead south, it was dead south! Right, here!

669
00:39:54,163 --> 00:39:58,163
んで道が、えー北、北、北…
And the road goes, um, north, north, north...

670
00:39:59,163 --> 00:40:02,163
ふんふんふん、こうした時に…
Uh-huh, uh-huh, looking this way...

671
00:40:02,163 --> 00:40:03,663
この辺か？
Around here?

672
00:40:03,963 --> 00:40:05,163
この辺…
Around here...

673
00:40:05,271 --> 00:40:05,871
...か。
...right?

674
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:08,071
のじゃ。
Alright.

675
00:40:10,071 --> 00:40:12,021
結構いいんじゃない？
Isn't this pretty good?

676
00:40:13,171 --> 00:40:15,121
結構いいんじゃないかわし。
Aren't I doing pretty well?

677
00:40:15,671 --> 00:40:18,571
のじゃーー！
Let's gooo!

678
00:40:18,621 --> 00:40:20,071
いわき市だった！
It was Iwaki City!

679
00:40:21,971 --> 00:40:24,071
0ってやっぱ難しいな、わし。
Getting a 0-meter distance is really tough.

680
00:40:24,121 --> 00:40:26,071
苦手なんだよな、0に置くの。
I'm so bad at pinpointing right on 0.

681
00:40:26,171 --> 00:40:28,571
ほら！いわき市って書いてる！
Look! It says Iwaki City!

682
00:40:28,871 --> 00:40:30,971
なんか平仮名3文字の市って、
When it's a three-character hiragana city name,

683
00:40:31,021 --> 00:40:34,971
遠くから見てさ、文字がさ視認できなくてもさ、
even looking from far away and you can't read the text...

684
00:40:35,321 --> 00:40:39,071
文字の視認ができなくてもさ、ここの「市」って漢字とさ、
Even if you can't read it, with the kanji for 'city' here,

685
00:40:39,121 --> 00:40:42,571
ここの3文字の密度が明らかにないから、
and the density of these three characters clearly being so low,

686
00:40:42,621 --> 00:40:45,121
平仮名だなーって思う。
you can tell it's hiragana.

687
00:40:45,171 --> 00:40:49,071
寒そうに見えないってどの辺で感じればいいか。えっと、
How could I tell it doesn't look cold? Well...

688
00:40:49,371 --> 00:40:51,471
ま、東北なんだけど、
Well, it is Tohoku, but...

689
00:40:51,571 --> 00:40:53,971
東北の割に、
for Tohoku...

690
00:40:54,021 --> 00:40:57,371
えっとまず、山がそんなないし、
First of all, there aren't many mountains,

691
00:40:57,671 --> 00:41:01,071
東北って結構どこでもごつごつ山がいっぱい見えるから、
and since you can usually see rugged mountains everywhere in Tohoku,

692
00:41:01,121 --> 00:41:04,971
東北であんま山見えないの珍しいなって思うのと、
it felt unusual not to see many mountains in Tohoku.

693
00:41:05,071 --> 00:41:09,571
あとね、その雪用にポールみたいなのが立ってない？
Also, don't they usually have snow poles set up?

694
00:41:10,271 --> 00:41:13,671
ポールみたいなのが立ってる気がするよ。
I feel like snow poles are usually standing there,

695
00:41:13,971 --> 00:41:16,071
で、なんか、寒いとこはね。
you know, in cold regions.

696
00:41:16,171 --> 00:41:21,971
そこでなんか車に「ここ、あの、道じゃないので注意なのじゃ」みたいなのが
They put up markers to warn cars like, 'Heads up, this isn't part of the road!'

697
00:41:22,171 --> 00:41:23,971
立ってて、
They stand there,

698
00:41:24,021 --> 00:41:27,571
あと空の色がね、東北の色じゃないんだよな。
and the color of the sky isn't a Tohoku sky.

699
00:41:27,671 --> 00:41:31,671
東北の空ってもうちょいね、彩度がね、低いのじゃ。
Tohoku's sky usually has lower saturation.

700
00:41:31,821 --> 00:41:34,971
東北にしてはね、澄んでるね。
For Tohoku, it's really clear.

701
00:41:35,021 --> 00:41:39,671
澄んでる青空じゃから、結構あったかそう。
Since it's a clear blue sky, it looks pretty warm.

702
00:41:40,171 --> 00:41:45,971
大体北陸とか東北って、空の色がね、だいたい曇ってんだよな。
In Hokuriku and Tohoku, the sky is mostly overcast.

703
00:41:46,171 --> 00:41:49,371
うん、大体曇ってる。うん。
Yeah, it's usually cloudy.

704
00:41:50,071 --> 00:41:51,971
から思うな。
That's why I thought so.

705
00:41:52,971 --> 00:41:55,671
あと何じゃろね、雪降らないの。
What else tells you it doesn't snow much?

706
00:41:56,071 --> 00:41:59,771
あ、東北だったらあと灯油タンクとかめっちゃ見えるかな。
Oh, in Tohoku you usually see lots of kerosene tanks.

707
00:41:59,971 --> 00:42:02,371
ま、この辺は二重じゃけど。
Well, these are double windows though.

708
00:42:02,971 --> 00:42:05,171
うーん、ぐらいかな。
Yeah... that's about it.

709
00:42:05,471 --> 00:42:09,971
ま、屋根とかもあんまなんか、そんな雪降りそうな感じの屋根ではない。
Also, the roofs don't really look like the heavy snowfall kind.

710
00:42:10,271 --> 00:42:12,671
山も緑緑だし。
The mountains are all green, too.

711
00:42:12,971 --> 00:42:15,671
雪山ないしな。
No snow on them either.

712
00:42:16,171 --> 00:42:19,171
うん。な気がする。
Yeah, that's what it feels like.

713
00:42:20,271 --> 00:42:21,571
うん。
Yeah.

714
00:42:22,171 --> 00:42:25,671
ま、二重丸のとこも多いよね。
Well, a lot of places have bullseye marks too.

715
00:42:26,171 --> 00:42:27,171
うん。
Yeah.

716
00:42:27,971 --> 00:42:32,571
からなんか、なのにこの東北のプレートがあって、「嘘でしょ？」
So when there was this Tohoku plate, I was like, 'No way!'

717
00:42:32,621 --> 00:42:35,571
この景...この空で、この空で東北？
With this scene... this sky, Tohoku with this sky?!

718
00:42:35,971 --> 00:42:41,671
って思ったときは、まあ、まあまず太平洋側、
When I thought that, my first thought was the Pacific coast,

719
00:42:41,771 --> 00:42:45,971
このギリ関東らへんの福島らへん。
around Fukushima, right on the border of Kanto.

720
00:42:46,371 --> 00:42:50,171
あと今回に関しては西側に山が結構見えた。
Also, in this round, I could see quite a few mountains to the west.

721
00:42:50,471 --> 00:42:56,671
西側には山見えるのに、東にはあんまそんなたくさん見えなかったから、わしの初期位置では。
I could see mountains to the west, but hardly any to the east from my starting position.

722
00:42:56,971 --> 00:43:01,671
だから、こっちに山ある太平洋側かな？って
So I thought, 'Mountains over here, so maybe the Pacific side?'

723
00:43:02,171 --> 00:43:04,971
思ったのじゃ。
That was my reasoning.

724
00:43:05,571 --> 00:43:09,771
のっちゃーー！次行くのっちゃーー！
Alright! Moving on to the next one!

725
00:43:09,871 --> 00:43:12,971
白上の湧水。
Shirakami Spring Water.

726
00:43:13,171 --> 00:43:14,771
私たちの名水。
'Our Famous Spring Water.'

727
00:43:14,871 --> 00:43:19,771
今日わしがアークでぐちゅぐちゅになってるときに助けてくれた？
Did that help me out earlier today when I was getting totally crushed in ARK?

728
00:43:20,171 --> 00:43:24,571
のじゃーー、ちょっ...ちょっと読めないか？
Let's see... Wait, can I not read this?

729
00:43:24,971 --> 00:43:27,171
ちょっと読みづらいか？
Is it a bit hard to read?

730
00:43:27,271 --> 00:43:29,171
なんちゃら県。
Something-prefecture.

731
00:43:29,271 --> 00:43:33,171
2文字、漢字2文字の県、どこにでもあるのじゃ。
A two-kanji prefecture... that could be anywhere!

732
00:43:33,171 --> 00:43:34,671
ふんふん。
Hmm, hmm.

733
00:43:34,771 --> 00:43:37,571
それでは、電柱などを見ていきますか。
Well then, let's look at the utility poles and such.

734
00:43:37,771 --> 00:43:39,371
東北だ。
It's Tohoku.

735
00:43:40,971 --> 00:43:43,171
東北としたときに、
Assuming it's Tohoku...

736
00:43:44,171 --> 00:43:45,971
なんだここ。
What's this place?

737
00:43:46,071 --> 00:43:48,171
待って、書いてあるし。
Wait, it's written right here!

738
00:43:48,171 --> 00:43:50,471
十和田市多くない？
Aren't there a lot of Towada Cities?

739
00:43:50,571 --> 00:43:54,371
りょ...りょ...いっぱいある！いっぱいあるよ！要素がいっぱいある！
So... so many clues! There are tons! So many hints!

740
00:43:54,371 --> 00:43:55,971
十和田市。
Towada City.

741
00:43:56,171 --> 00:43:58,171
十和田市でした。
It was Towada City.

742
00:43:59,771 --> 00:44:01,671
ふんふんふん。
Hmm, hmm, hmm.

743
00:44:01,771 --> 00:44:05,771
そして湧水。え、2個あるよ？ダブルコンボ。
And spring water. Wait, there are two? A double combo!

744
00:44:05,971 --> 00:44:07,671
ダブルコンボなのじゃ。
It's a double combo.

745
00:44:07,971 --> 00:44:10,671
湧水ってどっから見えるんやろな。
At what zoom level does spring water show up?

746
00:44:10,771 --> 00:44:12,571
湧水、これか？
Spring water... is this it?

747
00:44:12,671 --> 00:44:14,671
湧水これか？
Spring water, this one?

748
00:44:14,771 --> 00:44:16,971
流石にこれか？湧水。
Could this really be it? Spring water...

749
00:44:16,971 --> 00:44:19,471
でも「白神の」って書いてないよ。
But it doesn't say 'Shirakami'.

750
00:44:19,471 --> 00:44:22,471
書いてないけど、ウエスト方面にあるってことは、
It doesn't say it, but since it's toward the west,

751
00:44:22,571 --> 00:44:27,671
なんかこの辺から、この辺からくねくね行ってみたいな感じなんじゃないの？
doesn't that mean we wind around from somewhere over here?

752
00:44:28,171 --> 00:44:30,671
道がこうなってるじゃろ？
The road goes like this, right?

753
00:44:30,671 --> 00:44:32,071
北でしょ？
That's north, right?

754
00:44:32,071 --> 00:44:35,671
で、こういうくねっとした...
And then it curves like this...

755
00:44:35,971 --> 00:44:37,571
湧水どれや？
Which spring water is it?

756
00:44:37,571 --> 00:44:40,171
湧水これで、
If this is the spring water...

757
00:44:40,171 --> 00:44:43,371
いや、湧水いっぱいありそうだよな。
Actually, there are probably tons of springs.

758
00:44:43,471 --> 00:44:45,971
ちょっと、ちょっとムズいか。
Wait, is this a bit tricky?

759
00:44:46,671 --> 00:44:49,071
これは何神社なんだ？
What shrine is this?

760
00:44:49,171 --> 00:44:52,471
これの神社の名前が見えればいいんだけど。
If only I could see the name of this shrine.

761
00:44:52,571 --> 00:44:54,571
何神社なんじゃろな。
I wonder what shrine it is.

762
00:44:54,571 --> 00:44:56,671
漢字がちょっと、
The kanji is a bit...

763
00:44:56,971 --> 00:44:59,571
稲荷？稲荷？
Inari? Inari?

764
00:44:59,671 --> 00:45:02,171
2文字目が...
The second character...

765
00:45:02,171 --> 00:45:05,171
2文字目が荷物の「荷」に見える。
The second character looks like the 'ni' from 'nimotsu'.

766
00:45:06,479 --> 00:45:09,179
荷物の「荷」に見えるから…
Because it looks like the "ni" in "nimotsu"...

767
00:45:13,879 --> 00:45:16,379
確かにこの辺団地だな。し、
It's true there are housing complexes around here. And...

768
00:45:16,579 --> 00:45:18,379
この辺めっちゃ建物あるから、
...there are a lot of buildings around here,

769
00:45:18,579 --> 00:45:20,979
こんな山の中じゃない感じか？
...so maybe it's not deep in the mountains like this?

770
00:45:22,579 --> 00:45:24,579
稲荷に見えない？
Doesn't it look like "Inari"?

771
00:45:25,579 --> 00:45:27,979
わし稲荷に見えるんだけど…
To me, it looks like "Inari"...

772
00:45:30,379 --> 00:45:32,379
何色になってるんだろうな？
I wonder what color it shows up as...

773
00:45:32,579 --> 00:45:34,079
そういう…
That kind of...

774
00:45:34,979 --> 00:45:37,979
神社…稲荷、稲荷…
Shrine... Inari, Inari...

775
00:45:41,579 --> 00:45:44,379
ちょっとこっから見つけんのは、キツいか…
Finding it from here might be tough...

776
00:45:45,579 --> 00:45:48,379
こっから…こっからはキツいか…
From here... yeah, from here it's tough...

777
00:45:49,379 --> 00:45:52,979
山とか…でもね、ここね高いんだよね、場所が。
Mountains or... but you know, this location is high up.

778
00:45:53,479 --> 00:45:57,979
そもそもここが、かなり高地な予感。空近いし…
I have a feeling this place is on pretty high ground to begin with. The sky is close...

779
00:45:59,179 --> 00:46:03,379
ここがそもそも結構山の上目な方だなと思っているため…
Since I'm thinking this spot is already pretty high up the mountain...

780
00:46:03,579 --> 00:46:05,779
で南が多分下か。
And south is probably downhill.

781
00:46:06,179 --> 00:46:10,179
うん、山の上目なほうな予感がしているので…
Yeah, I have a feeling it's on the higher side of the mountain, so...

782
00:46:10,679 --> 00:46:15,979
なんか市街地…超市街地じゃないと思っていて。これ見ればいいのか？内水面研究所みたいな…
I don't think it's an urban... super urban area. Should I look for this? Like "Inland Water Fisheries Research Institute"...

783
00:46:16,379 --> 00:46:18,679
研究所見つければいいのか？
Should I just look for the research institute?

784
00:46:19,379 --> 00:46:21,379
研究所見つけたいな。
I'd love to find the research institute.

785
00:46:22,379 --> 00:46:23,679
神社…
Shrine...

786
00:46:24,179 --> 00:46:28,179
うん、やっぱ稲荷って書いてるように見えるんだけどなわしには。
Yeah, to me it really looks like it says "Inari", though.

787
00:46:28,379 --> 00:46:30,179
研究所を見つけたい。
I want to find the research institute.

788
00:46:30,779 --> 00:46:34,179
研究所はござりませぬか〜？
Is there no research institute around here~?

789
00:46:37,179 --> 00:46:39,179
内水面…
Inland water...

790
00:46:39,979 --> 00:46:44,679
内水面研究所…研究所の香りがあんまりしないなあ。
Inland Water Fisheries Research Institute... I'm not really getting a research institute vibe here.

791
00:46:45,179 --> 00:46:47,679
研究所の香りって何だがち。
What does a research institute vibe even mean, lol.

792
00:46:48,179 --> 00:46:51,679
神社とかを見つけられればいいんじゃけどなあ。
If only I could find a shrine or something...

793
00:46:52,479 --> 00:46:56,379
でもこの辺でさあ、高めになっててさあ、
But around here, it's on higher ground...

794
00:46:56,779 --> 00:47:01,379
研究所があってってなると結構絞られそうじゃけど…
...and having a research institute should narrow it down quite a bit, though...

795
00:47:05,179 --> 00:47:11,179
うーん…ちょっと沼か？ちょっと沼か？
Hmm... Am I getting stuck in a rabbit hole? Stuck in a loop?

796
00:47:12,179 --> 00:47:16,979
見てはいますが…いますが…
I am looking, but... looking, but...

797
00:47:17,579 --> 00:47:20,679
発電所…稲…
Power station... Ina...

798
00:47:20,979 --> 00:47:23,679
「稲」つくよ。「稲」だけじゃダメか。
It starts with "Ina". Is just "Ina" not enough?

799
00:47:24,579 --> 00:47:29,179
うーん…上下水、道…ふんふんふん…
Hmm... Water and sewage... hm, hm, hm...

800
00:47:32,179 --> 00:47:35,179
矢神、八反…うーん…
Yagami, Hattan... hmm...

801
00:47:35,579 --> 00:47:38,379
稲荷神社がないなあ。
There's no Inari Shrine...

802
00:47:38,579 --> 00:47:40,679
てか神社多くないか？
Wait, aren't there a lot of shrines?

803
00:47:41,179 --> 00:47:44,179
神社めちゃくちゃないかこの辺？
Aren't there an insane number of shrines around here?

804
00:47:44,979 --> 00:47:47,679
めちゃくちゃあるな…
There really are a ton...

805
00:47:51,179 --> 00:47:54,979
名水…白上の湧水…
Famous spring water... Shirakami spring water...

806
00:47:56,179 --> 00:48:01,679
いやなんか水水言う…水水こんな言うなら…
Man, they keep mentioning "water"... If it's this obsessed with water...

807
00:48:02,179 --> 00:48:03,379
ねえ？
...right?

808
00:48:04,679 --> 00:48:09,679
結構水が湧きそうな辺りにあってほしいものですけど…
I'd expect it to be in an area where water naturally springs up, but...

809
00:48:10,179 --> 00:48:12,679
ものじゃけど…
...though that should be the case...

810
00:48:13,179 --> 00:48:18,379
ここまで…ここまで森じゃないか流石に。
Not quite... it surely isn't this deep in the forest.

811
00:48:19,379 --> 00:48:23,679
でなんか水が結構いい感じの水がいっぱい採れる場所だから、なんか貯水…
And since it's a place where you can get plenty of really good water, maybe water storage...

812
00:48:23,979 --> 00:48:31,679
貯水できそうな場所とかが相応しいかなとは思いつつ…思いつつ…
...somewhere suitable for water storage might fit, while I think that... while I think that...

813
00:48:33,179 --> 00:48:37,179
水道…やっぱ水に関する設備が多いなあ。
Waterworks... There really are a lot of water-related facilities.

814
00:48:37,779 --> 00:48:41,679
うちない…研究所…ふんふんふん…
Uchinai... Research institute... Hm, hm, hm...

815
00:48:42,179 --> 00:48:45,679
「過去に何か多かった場所に神社が多くなる」…やっぱあれかな？
"Shrines are plentiful in places where something occurred often in the past"... I wonder if it's that?

816
00:48:45,979 --> 00:48:54,179
やっぱ水とかさあ、ため池とかでっかい湖とかそういうのが多かったから、結構水害とかが多かったのかしら。
Because of all the water, reservoirs, big lakes and such, maybe there used to be a lot of flood disasters?

817
00:48:55,179 --> 00:48:59,179
井戸…井戸、井戸、井戸…
Well... Well, well, well...

818
00:49:00,179 --> 00:49:03,679
確かに山とかもね結構信仰心…そうだよなあ。
True, mountains also attract a lot of religious devotion... That makes sense.

819
00:49:04,179 --> 00:49:06,179
うん、うん、うん。
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

820
00:49:08,679 --> 00:49:10,179
なくね？
Isn't it just not here?

821
00:49:10,679 --> 00:49:16,979
結構チラチラしてはいるが…いるのじゃが…いるのじゃが…
I've been glancing around quite a bit, but... but... but...

822
00:49:17,979 --> 00:49:19,379
うーん…
Hmm...

823
00:49:20,679 --> 00:49:23,679
ちょっとじゃあ施設を探すのは諦めて、
Alright then, let's give up on searching for facilities...

824
00:49:24,579 --> 00:49:27,179
街とかの感じで見るか。
...and look at the layout of the towns.

825
00:49:27,679 --> 00:49:30,679
予想なんだけど…
Just my guess, but...

826
00:49:30,979 --> 00:49:33,679
こっちが市街地で…
This side is urban...

827
00:49:33,979 --> 00:49:39,179
多分この辺？こっちが市街地で、こういう高いところにある気がしていて…
Maybe around here? With the city over here, I feel like we're somewhere high up like this...

828
00:49:39,679 --> 00:49:42,179
うん、こっちが市街地な気がする。
Yeah, feels like this direction is the city.

829
00:49:42,179 --> 00:49:46,679
で、こっちにもうちょい栄えてる目の何かが、あるみたいな。
And over here, there's something that seems a bit more developed.

830
00:49:46,979 --> 00:49:50,179
こういうとこ？こういうとこな気がする。
A spot like this? I feel like it's a place like this.

831
00:49:50,679 --> 00:49:53,979
んで…SW…W…
And... southwest... west...

832
00:49:54,979 --> 00:50:01,679
うーん、こっち側も結構低めの土地になってるのも気になってはいるな。じゃから、なんかこの辺とか？
Hmm, it also bothers me that this side is relatively low-lying terrain. So maybe around here?

833
00:50:01,979 --> 00:50:04,379
いやもっと奥かなあ？ちょっとわかんないんじゃけど置いてみよ。
Or maybe further inland? I'm not really sure, but let's place my guess.

834
00:50:04,987 --> 00:50:05,887
のじゃー！
Noja~!

835
00:50:05,887 --> 00:50:08,587
え、めっちゃ、めっちゃ、なんか、違う！
Huh, it's way, way... completely different!

836
00:50:08,987 --> 00:50:11,087
思ってた所と全然違う！
It's completely different from where I thought!

837
00:50:11,187 --> 00:50:13,187
思ってた所と全然違うのじゃ。
It's totally different from where I thought, noja.

838
00:50:13,187 --> 00:50:16,487
めっちゃ、本当だ、白神稲荷神社ある！
Wow, for real, there is a Shirakami Inari Shrine!

839
00:50:17,087 --> 00:50:20,487
めっちゃ南、東、南東だ！
It's way south... east, southeast!

840
00:50:21,187 --> 00:50:24,587
おっと、ちょっと、もう一回考えさせてください。
Oops, wait, let me think this through one more time.

841
00:50:25,087 --> 00:50:27,587
ここ、としたときに、
If that was the spot...

842
00:50:28,087 --> 00:50:31,487
え、じゃあ、十和田市って全体的に高いのか？
Wait, then is Towada City situated high up overall?

843
00:50:31,587 --> 00:50:34,087
全体的に高い位置なのか？
Is it situated at a higher elevation in general?

844
00:50:34,587 --> 00:50:38,987
だってさ、ええと、こっちが北でしょ？
Because, let's see, this way is north, right?

845
00:50:39,387 --> 00:50:40,887
東でしょ？
That's east, right?

846
00:50:40,987 --> 00:50:43,987
東がめっちゃ低くなってるのなんでだ？
Why does it get so much lower to the east?

847
00:50:44,087 --> 00:50:47,887
この東がめちゃくちゃ開けてるのはなんでじゃ？
Why is it so wide open to the east, noja?

848
00:50:48,087 --> 00:50:51,087
ここが平野すぎるからか？ここめっちゃ平野なのか？
Is it because it's too flat? Are there huge plains here?

849
00:50:51,387 --> 00:50:52,887
んで、東でしょ？
And then that's east, right?

850
00:50:53,287 --> 00:50:54,587
西。
West.

851
00:50:55,587 --> 00:50:58,387
西も、なんか、この辺めっちゃ開けてない？
To the west too, isn't it super wide open around here?

852
00:50:58,487 --> 00:51:01,087
全体的に高いだけなのかな？
Maybe it's just that the whole area is elevated?

853
00:51:01,487 --> 00:51:02,787
ほんで、
And then...

854
00:51:02,887 --> 00:51:04,087
南。
South.

855
00:51:04,087 --> 00:51:05,087
南。
South.

856
00:51:05,387 --> 00:51:06,587
南。
South.

857
00:51:07,087 --> 00:51:09,587
市街地、北なんだね。
The urban center is to the north, huh.

858
00:51:10,087 --> 00:51:13,587
わしたちが見えてた、なんか団地っぽいのは多分この辺で、
Those housing complex-looking buildings we saw were probably around here...

859
00:51:13,787 --> 00:51:15,487
あれね。
Yeah, those.

860
00:51:15,587 --> 00:51:19,587
あっちが、え、高いほうに行ったほうが市街地なことあるんだ。
Over there... Huh, so the urban area can actually be in the higher elevation area.

861
00:51:19,587 --> 00:51:23,087
なんかさ、市街地がさ、本当だ、結構、結構街だな。
The urban area... Oh wow, it really is quite a town.

862
00:51:23,587 --> 00:51:25,487
なんかその、なんじゃろうな。
What can I say...

863
00:51:25,587 --> 00:51:30,587
市街地ってさ、結構さ、低めの場所にあるイメージ。というか、なんか
I had this image of urban areas being in lower places. Or rather...

864
00:51:30,587 --> 00:51:35,087
山の上にあんまり家とかって建てられないイメージで、やっぱ平野のほうが住みやすいから、
My impression was that you don't build many houses on mountains, and plains are easier to live on,

865
00:51:35,587 --> 00:51:38,087
住みやすいから、
so because it's easier to live there...

866
00:51:39,087 --> 00:51:41,487
その、イメージ的にはというか、
Well, in terms of my image of it, or...

867
00:51:41,587 --> 00:51:46,587
なんじゃろ、高くなってたら、あ、下のほうに街があるんだなって思っちゃうんだけど、
how to put it, if it's elevated, I tend to think the town would be down below, but...

868
00:51:46,987 --> 00:51:48,587
台地だな。
It's a plateau.

869
00:51:49,087 --> 00:51:51,087
しか、あ、そうじゃの。
But, oh, that makes sense.

870
00:51:51,087 --> 00:51:57,087
多分川とか、さっきあの神社がいっぱいあるね、水害とかなのかなみたいな話をしたのもあるし、
Maybe with the river, and like we talked about earlier with all those shrines, wondering if there were floods...

871
00:51:57,087 --> 00:51:59,087
多分、うん。
Probably, yeah.

872
00:51:59,087 --> 00:52:01,587
水害が多かったのかな？
Maybe there used to be a lot of flood damage?

873
00:52:01,587 --> 00:52:07,087
山から流れる水とかでの土砂崩れとか、そういう系が多かった感じか？
Like landslides caused by water flowing from the mountains, stuff like that was frequent?

874
00:52:07,087 --> 00:52:09,087
だから、
That's why...

875
00:52:09,587 --> 00:52:12,587
低いところだと住めないのか。
you couldn't live in the lower areas.

876
00:52:13,087 --> 00:52:15,587
盆地みたいな感じ？うーん。
Like a basin? Hmm...

877
00:52:16,387 --> 00:52:18,087
なるほどね。
I see.

878
00:52:18,587 --> 00:52:24,587
そっか、川とかの影響で、川が溢れちゃった時とか、増水しちゃった時とかが危ないから、
Right, because of rivers, it's dangerous when rivers overflow or the water level rises,

879
00:52:25,087 --> 00:52:26,487
だから、
so...

880
00:52:26,587 --> 00:52:29,587
だから高めのところに住んでるのかな？
that's why they live up on higher ground?

881
00:52:30,587 --> 00:52:32,087
うん、結構かもね。
Yeah, that could very well be it.

882
00:52:32,587 --> 00:52:36,587
整備されてないとか、そのまんまの川っぽい。
It's not reinforced or anything, looks like a completely natural river.

883
00:52:38,587 --> 00:52:40,087
そうかも。
That might be it.

884
00:52:40,087 --> 00:52:43,087
酷い水害が多いと高い所に住宅地。
If there's severe flooding, residential areas are placed on high ground.

885
00:52:43,087 --> 00:52:47,087
やっぱなんか、異様に神社の数が多いし、
There really is an unusually large number of shrines,

886
00:52:47,587 --> 00:52:50,587
そういうのがあったのかもしれないのじゃ。
so maybe something like that happened, noja.

887
00:52:51,087 --> 00:52:53,587
可能性としてね、ね。
Just as a possibility, right?

888
00:52:54,587 --> 00:52:58,087
内水研究、そのための？
Inland water research... for that purpose?

889
00:52:58,087 --> 00:53:00,587
確かに、研究所あったよね。
There was indeed a research lab, wasn't there?

890
00:53:00,587 --> 00:53:01,587
どこじゃっけ？
Where was it?

891
00:53:02,087 --> 00:53:03,587
ここか。
Here, huh.

892
00:53:03,587 --> 00:53:09,587
青森県産業技術センター内、水面、内水面研究所。
Inside Aomori Prefectural Industrial Technology Center, Water Surface... Inland Water Fisheries Research Institute.

893
00:53:10,087 --> 00:53:12,587
ここに湧き水が、へえー。
Spring water is here? Huh.

894
00:53:12,587 --> 00:53:15,087
湧き水っつってもあれなんだ。
Even though it's called spring water, it's like that.

895
00:53:15,587 --> 00:53:18,587
なんか、そんなにめちゃくちゃ貯水池というよりかは、
Rather than a massive reservoir,

896
00:53:18,587 --> 00:53:21,087
ちょっとここ歩いて行ってみたいの。
I kind of want to walk over and see it.

897
00:53:21,587 --> 00:53:24,587
湧き水、白神の湧き水。
Spring water... Shirakami spring water.

898
00:53:24,587 --> 00:53:26,087
見てみるか。
Let's take a look.

899
00:53:26,087 --> 00:53:28,087
ここやろ？神社。
It's here, right? The shrine.

900
00:53:28,087 --> 00:53:30,087
ああ、湧き水！
Ah, spring water!

901
00:53:30,087 --> 00:53:34,587
本当になんか、湧き水って名前にふさわしいぐらいのサイズ感だな。
It's really just the right size to be called a spring.

902
00:53:35,087 --> 00:53:40,087
なんか貯水池みたいな感じなのかなって思ったんじゃけど、貯水池というよりは本当に田んぼが作れそうなぐらいの、
I thought it might be something like a reservoir, but rather than that, it's just about big enough to make a rice paddy...

903
00:53:40,587 --> 00:53:41,587
うん。
Yeah.

904
00:53:42,087 --> 00:53:47,087
田んぼが作れそうなぐらいの、ちょっとした、水？
Just enough water to make a rice paddy, perhaps?

905
00:53:48,887 --> 00:53:51,387
うん、ちょっとした水だな。
Yeah, it's just a modest body of water.

906
00:53:51,487 --> 00:53:55,087
ふん、ふん、ふん。
Mhm, mhm, mhm.

907
00:53:55,587 --> 00:53:57,087
なるほどねー。
I see...

908
00:53:58,587 --> 00:54:06,587
いや、わしが想像したなんか、結構でかめな貯水池とか川なのかなとか、そう、池とかなのかなみたいな思ってたけど、
I imagined something pretty huge like a reservoir or a river, or yeah, a large pond, but...

909
00:54:07,087 --> 00:54:10,087
本当にちょこっとな感じなんじゃの。
It's really just a small spot, noja.

910
00:54:10,587 --> 00:54:14,587
神社の中の湧き水ってめっちゃ幻想的なのじゃ。
Spring water inside a shrine is super magical, noja.

911
00:54:15,087 --> 00:54:16,087
うん。
Yeah.

912
00:54:16,087 --> 00:54:19,087
ね、じわじわ出てる感じの。
Right? Like it's gently bubbling up.

913
00:54:19,087 --> 00:54:21,087
綺麗な場所じゃの。
It's a beautiful place, noja.

914
00:54:21,087 --> 00:54:24,087
湧水？湧水って読むんだ。
"Yūsui"? Ah, you read it as "yūsui."

915
00:54:24,587 --> 00:54:26,587
湧水なのか。
So it's "yūsui."

916
00:54:26,587 --> 00:54:28,587
へえー。
Wow.

917
00:54:30,087 --> 00:54:33,587
なるほどねー、神秘的なのじゃ。
I see... it's quite mystical, noja.

918
00:54:34,887 --> 00:54:38,587
あ、「ときの広場」来た、「ときの広場」！
Ah, "Toki no Hiroba" came up! Toki no Hiroba!

919
00:54:39,587 --> 00:54:41,587
ときの広場や。
It's Toki no Hiroba.

920
00:54:42,087 --> 00:54:43,087
電力見る？
Should we check the power company?

921
00:54:43,587 --> 00:54:45,587
東京電力なのじゃ！
It's Tokyo Electric Power, noja!

922
00:54:46,587 --> 00:54:48,087
ときの広場来たよ。
We got Toki no Hiroba.

923
00:54:48,087 --> 00:54:50,087
そら先輩なのじゃ。
It's Sora-senpai, noja!

924
00:54:51,587 --> 00:54:53,087
さて。
Now then...

925
00:54:53,587 --> 00:54:58,087
道を見た時に、東京電力で、
Looking at the road... it's Tokyo Electric Power, and...

926
00:54:58,087 --> 00:54:59,587
何て書いてある？
what does it say?

927
00:54:59,587 --> 00:55:01,587
何とか神社通り。
Something Shrine Dori.

928
00:55:01,587 --> 00:55:03,587
何とか神社通り。
Something Shrine Dori.

929
00:55:03,587 --> 00:55:05,087
なんか、隣...
Like, next door...

930
00:55:05,195 --> 00:55:07,045
ぽい香りあり。
...-esque scent detected.

931
00:55:08,015 --> 00:55:09,095
都内?
Within Tokyo?

932
00:55:10,045 --> 00:55:12,945
うん、と、東京っぽい香りあり。
Yeah, it has a Tokyo-esque scent.

933
00:55:13,545 --> 00:55:15,695
なんかさあ...
Like, you know...

934
00:55:17,495 --> 00:55:18,995
ん、なんじゃろうなあ...
Hmm, what could it be...

935
00:55:22,045 --> 00:55:23,845
なんかこういうさあ...
Like, when you look at this...

936
00:55:24,595 --> 00:55:28,145
こういうの見るとさあ、わかるかなあ?
When you see this kind of scenery, you know what I mean?

937
00:55:28,695 --> 00:55:32,645
なんか西、西東京とかに置きたくなっちゃう。
It makes me want to drop the pin in West Tokyo.

938
00:55:32,795 --> 00:55:35,995
雰囲気ね。完全に雰囲気なんじゃけど。
Just the vibe, you know. Purely based on vibes, though.

939
00:55:36,245 --> 00:55:38,945
なんか西東京っぽくない?
Doesn't it feel like West Tokyo?

940
00:55:39,995 --> 00:55:42,145
西東京の香りする。
I smell West Tokyo.

941
00:55:42,295 --> 00:55:45,595
これがちょっと見えないんだよなあ。何通りって書いてあるんだろう?
I can't really read this, though. What street does it say it is?

942
00:55:45,695 --> 00:55:47,645
なんとか神社通り。
...Something Shrine Street.

943
00:55:47,795 --> 00:55:50,145
なんとか神社通りって書いてある。
It says "...something Shrine Street."

944
00:55:51,495 --> 00:55:53,945
ん、ちょっと西東京の香りする。
Yeah, it has a bit of a West Tokyo scent.

945
00:55:54,195 --> 00:55:55,695
時の広場...
Toki no Hiroba...

946
00:55:56,395 --> 00:56:00,845
それ以上はちょっと情報があまり取れない。
Beyond that, I can't really get much info.

947
00:56:01,695 --> 00:56:04,995
こっちに社会あり。
There's civilization over this way.

948
00:56:05,995 --> 00:56:08,395
こっちに社会ありだが、
There's civilization over here, but...

949
00:56:08,595 --> 00:56:11,945
時の広場ってそんなでっかくは書いてないか。
I guess "Toki no Hiroba" wouldn't be written very big on the map.

950
00:56:12,195 --> 00:56:12,995
うーん...
Hmm...

951
00:56:13,595 --> 00:56:15,695
ちょ、一旦押してみるか。のじゃ!
Let's just give it a click. There!

952
00:56:16,395 --> 00:56:18,345
もっと西だ!
It was even further west!

953
00:56:18,495 --> 00:56:20,145
もっともっと西だ!
Way, way further west!

954
00:56:21,995 --> 00:56:24,095
ここでした。ときの...
It was right here. Toki no...

955
00:56:24,595 --> 00:56:26,195
時の広場...
Toki no Hiroba...

956
00:56:26,195 --> 00:56:31,145
時の広場っていう名前の公園...
A park named Toki no Hiroba...

957
00:56:31,195 --> 00:56:32,395
公園なんだ。
So it's a park.

958
00:56:33,295 --> 00:56:34,395
割と...
Relatively...

959
00:56:34,995 --> 00:56:36,595
でもありじゃのう、
Still, it makes sense,

960
00:56:36,595 --> 00:56:39,195
多摩川より西じゃのう。
it's west of the Tama River.

961
00:56:40,495 --> 00:56:45,995
確かに。ここまで、ここまで内側じゃないか。この辺だったらもうちょい高い建物いっぱいあるか。
True. It wouldn't be this far in. If it were around here, there'd be more tall buildings.

962
00:56:46,095 --> 00:56:47,695
もうちょいあるか。
There'd be a few more.

963
00:56:49,395 --> 00:56:52,445
香りがさあ、西東京の香りするんだよなあ。
The scent, you know, it really smelled like West Tokyo.

964
00:56:52,495 --> 00:56:56,195
なんだろう、この西東京の香りって。
I wonder what this "West Tokyo scent" actually is.

965
00:56:58,195 --> 00:56:59,595
なんじゃろうね。
I wonder.

966
00:56:59,795 --> 00:57:05,695
なんかねえ、一軒家の感じがねえ、西東京なんだよねえ。
Like, you know, the vibe of the detached houses just screams West Tokyo.

967
00:57:06,995 --> 00:57:09,345
建ってある家の感じ?
The style of the houses built there?

968
00:57:09,395 --> 00:57:14,645
建ってある家の感じがさあ、西東京のそれなんだよなあ。
The style of the houses built there is totally that West Tokyo style.

969
00:57:14,695 --> 00:57:19,495
あとなんかこの、東京っぽいけど高い建物がない感じ?
Plus, that feeling of "it feels like Tokyo, but there aren't tall buildings"?

970
00:57:20,695 --> 00:57:21,995
うーん。
Hmm.

971
00:57:22,495 --> 00:57:27,195
なんか、なんかこの住宅街の感じが...
Somehow, the look of this residential area...

972
00:57:27,595 --> 00:57:31,695
西タウンっぽい... 西た- 西と混ざった。
feels like a west town... West to- "West" got mixed in.

973
00:57:31,695 --> 00:57:33,195
にし、西東京っぽい。
We- West Tokyo-esque.

974
00:57:33,195 --> 00:57:34,995
なんじゃろうね。
Wonder why.

975
00:57:35,995 --> 00:57:37,595
次行こうじゃ!
Let's move on to the next one!

976
00:57:38,395 --> 00:57:40,495
ふんぶんぶ...
Hunbunbu...

977
00:57:41,295 --> 00:57:42,595
ふんぶんぶ?
Hunbunbu?

978
00:57:44,295 --> 00:57:45,595
ふんぶ?
Hunbu?

979
00:57:46,095 --> 00:57:49,145
なんかすごい坂。なんかすごい坂。
That's quite a slope. What a steep slope.

980
00:57:49,195 --> 00:57:50,445
なんだ?
What's this?

981
00:57:50,495 --> 00:57:52,495
なんだここ? わしの知らない景色。
What is this place? A scenery I don't know.

982
00:57:52,595 --> 00:57:55,995
わしの知らない景色。え、何ここ?
A scenery I don't know. Wait, what is this place?

983
00:57:55,995 --> 00:57:58,495
わしがあんま見たことないタイプの景色。
A type of scenery I haven't seen much of.

984
00:57:58,495 --> 00:58:01,695
広馬場町。広馬場町。
Hirobaba-machi. Hirobaba-machi.

985
00:58:03,395 --> 00:58:04,395
ほう。
Oho.

986
00:58:04,595 --> 00:58:06,145
095。
095.

987
00:58:06,495 --> 00:58:09,195
095、本当にお前095合ってるんか?
095... Are you sure 095 is right?

988
00:58:09,495 --> 00:58:12,145
095ってこっちの方じゃなかったっけ?
Wasn't 095 over in this area?

989
00:58:12,295 --> 00:58:14,395
095ってこっちの方のイメージ。
I associate 095 with this region.

990
00:58:15,995 --> 00:58:20,695
あー、までも確かに、長崎なら確かにそうかも。長崎っぽさはある。
Ah, but yeah, if it's Nagasaki, that might make sense. It definitely has a Nagasaki feel.

991
00:58:21,995 --> 00:58:27,195
なんかこの坂の感じとかね。この坂の感じとか道の感じとか。
Like the feel of these slopes. The feel of the slopes and the streets.

992
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:31,695
長崎っぽいな。本当にそうかわかんないけど。
Very Nagasaki-like. Not that I know for sure, though.

993
00:58:32,295 --> 00:58:35,295
うん、なんか長崎って言われたらちょっと納得できる。
Yeah, if someone told me it's Nagasaki, I could buy that.

994
00:58:35,595 --> 00:58:38,595
ちょっとちゃんと見えないな。ちゃんと見えない。電柱が見たいの。
I can't quite see it properly. Can't see it properly. I want to see the utility pole.

995
00:58:39,795 --> 00:58:42,195
電柱が見たいんじゃが...
I really want to see the utility pole, but...

996
00:58:43,195 --> 00:58:44,995
見えないですね。
I can't see it.

997
00:58:46,995 --> 00:58:51,995
うん、でもこの坂の感じがちょっと長崎っぽいなって言われたら、わかる。
Yeah, but if someone told me this sloped look is a bit like Nagasaki, I'd get it.

998
00:58:52,595 --> 00:58:53,995
わかる。
I'd get it.

999
00:58:57,395 --> 00:59:00,845
なんだ? 見づらいな。これは違うか。
What's that? Hard to see. Is this not it?

1000
00:59:00,895 --> 00:59:02,195
建築会社か。
A construction company?

1001
00:59:02,395 --> 00:59:07,695
十八親和銀行。十八親和銀行。
Juhachi Shinwa Bank. Juhachi Shinwa Bank.

1002
00:59:08,195 --> 00:59:12,195
広馬場... 広馬場薬局。やっぱ広馬場...
Hirobaba... Hirobaba Pharmacy. So it really is Hirobaba...

1003
00:59:12,995 --> 00:59:14,695
広馬場なんだ。
It is Hirobaba.

1004
00:59:15,195 --> 00:59:17,195
広馬場は...
Hirobaba is...

1005
00:59:17,995 --> 00:59:21,195
広馬場あんま知らないけどわし。行けるかな?
I don't really know Hirobaba, though. Can I find it?

1006
00:59:22,195 --> 00:59:25,695
長崎全然詳しくないんだよな。広馬場...
I don't know Nagasaki well at all. Hirobaba...

1007
00:59:28,195 --> 00:59:33,195
やっぱ海、海近? 海近でくねくね...
Is it near the sea, after all? By the sea and curvy...

1008
00:59:33,995 --> 00:59:37,595
くねくねなとこの予感。
I feel like it's somewhere winding.

1009
00:59:38,895 --> 00:59:41,195
平... 平...
Hira... Hira...

1010
00:59:41,395 --> 00:59:43,395
他になんか情報ないかな?
Is there any other info?

1011
00:59:44,595 --> 00:59:47,995
こっちにちょっ... こっち... いやー、ちょっと...
Over this way a bit... Over here... No, wait...

1012
00:59:48,195 --> 00:59:50,495
海の香りを感じ取れない。
I can't smell the sea.

1013
00:59:50,495 --> 00:59:52,495
あるとしたらこっち...
If there were any, it'd be this way...

1014
00:59:52,495 --> 00:59:55,645
あるとしたらこっちじゃけどあんまり感じ取れない。
If anywhere, it'd be this way, but I can hardly sense it.

1015
00:59:55,695 --> 00:59:58,795
この山なんだ? NWの。
What's this mountain? To the northwest.

1016
00:59:59,195 --> 01:00:01,195
この山なんだ?
What mountain is this?

1017
01:00:01,695 --> 01:00:04,895
長崎の...
Nagasaki's...

1018
01:00:05,323 --> 01:00:07,743
わし長崎あんまわかんないからさ
I don't know Nagasaki very well...

1019
01:00:08,343 --> 01:00:11,383
長崎のさ市街、超市街じゃないさ、
So when it comes to areas of Nagasaki that aren't super downtown,

1020
01:00:11,383 --> 01:00:14,423
とこがさ、あんまりわかんないんだよな。
I don't really know them at all.

1021
01:00:15,983 --> 01:00:17,683
広馬場
Hirobaba...

1022
01:00:19,163 --> 01:00:21,203
え、広馬場？
Wait, Hirobaba?

1023
01:00:22,043 --> 01:00:24,123
え、海の香り感じとれない。
Huh, I can't smell any ocean breeze.

1024
01:00:24,703 --> 01:00:27,043
わしまだまだだな。
I've still got a long way to go.

1025
01:00:27,743 --> 01:00:31,643
わしまだまだかも。海の香りそんなわかんないな。
Maybe I still have a long way to go. I can't really sense the ocean.

1026
01:00:32,943 --> 01:00:37,023
しかも長崎って結構広いからな。
Besides, Nagasaki is pretty large, after all.

1027
01:00:37,643 --> 01:00:40,583
長崎内でも結構、
Even within Nagasaki Prefecture,

1028
01:00:42,723 --> 01:00:44,423
結構なんだよな。
there's quite a lot to it.

1029
01:00:45,643 --> 01:00:48,943
広馬場町を見つけられたら熱いんだけど。
It'd be huge if I could find Hirobaba-machi, though.

1030
01:00:49,443 --> 01:00:53,023
広馬場町結構そんな大きめじゃなさそうだから
Hirobaba-machi doesn't look like it's that big of a district,

1031
01:00:53,443 --> 01:00:57,243
パッと見つけられなさそうな予感。
so I have a feeling I won't easily spot it.

1032
01:00:58,843 --> 01:01:02,343
うーん、あんまパッとは見つけられなさそう。
Yeah, it doesn't look like something I can easily spot at a glance.

1033
01:01:02,503 --> 01:01:04,843
じゃし、長崎で...
And in Nagasaki...

1034
01:01:08,443 --> 01:01:13,743
結構ぎゅうぎゅうの、ぎゅうぎゅうのさ
There's a pretty packed, packed...

1035
01:01:15,243 --> 01:01:21,843
街ぎゅうぎゅうじゃん？じゃから結構人口密度高め、高めな場所なんだろうなと思うんだけど、
